[{:adr/distinctive-checks-6920 "wrong-engagement-type-violations is a genuinely NEW check kind for this fleet: a type-tag validity check (audit-opinion/issue must target :engagement-type :audit; tax-filing/submit must target :tax-filing), neither arithmetic nor party-screening. trial-balance-out-of-balance-violations extends 6492's pure-ground-truth-recompute family to an EQUALITY-OF-SUMS arithmetic shape (assets = liabilities + equity), a sixth domain-specific formula and a new arithmetic flavor within that family", :adr/bug-found-and-fixed-6920 "both the advisor's propose-audit-opinion and the governor's own trial-balance-out-of-balance-violations initially called trial-balance-difference unconditionally for :audit-opinion/issue, crashing with a NullPointerException when the target engagement was actually a :tax-filing engagement (no assets/liabilities/equity fields at all). Fixed in BOTH places by guarding the recompute on :engagement-type :audit first. Lesson: when a pure ground-truth recompute's inputs are only meaningful for a subset of an entity's type tags, both the advisor AND the governor must guard on the type tag before touching type-specific fields", :adr/pattern-6920 "sealed Ledger-LLM advisor + independent Audit Independence Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all ten prior actors; the FIRST professional-services vertical (ISIC division 69) in this fleet; THIRD build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492)", :adr/related ["2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520/6530/6820/6612/6492 ADR-0001s" "langgraph-clj ADR-0001"], :adr/no-capability-lib-6920 "unlike every prior actor in this fleet, this vertical's engagement records are practice-specific rather than a shared cross-operator data contract -- runs on the generic identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack only, per the blueprint's own explicit statement", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607071351", :adr/independence-reuse-6920 "independence-violation-violations reuses the unconditional-evaluation discipline (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations) citing the accounting profession's own specific regulatory term (auditor independence, AICPA/PCAOB/FRC/WPK), an honest reflection of how this concept is actually named and regulated in this profession", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 16, :blueprint 81, :spec 546, :total 643}", :adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true, :adr/dual-actuation-6920 "two actuation events (:actuation/issue-opinion, :actuation/submit-filing), matching 6512's/6622's/6520's/6530's/6820's dual-actuation shape", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 17, :blueprint 80, :spec 546, :total 643}", :adr/date "2026-07-07", :adr/test-status-6920 "38 tests / 172 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (two clean lifecycles + six HARD-hold cases, all correct after the NullPointerException fix)", :adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR, not an addendum to ADR-2607071250/ADR-2607071320/ADR-2607032000, because ISIC 6920 (division 69 professional services) is outside all three of those ADRs' explicit scopes, even though it shares the identical governed-actor pattern", :db/id -1, :adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-6920", :adr/guard-design-6920 "double-issuance/double-filing guards check dedicated boolean facts (:opinion-issued?/:filing-submitted?) rather than a :status value -- a design choice deliberately informed by 6492's status-lifecycle bug, not merely reused by analogy (the exact failure mode that caused that bug in the first place)", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-6920 (accounting, bookkeeping and auditing) deepened to :implemented -- first professional-services vertical"}]